  "ProjectionNotes": [
    "Source positions are zero-based native Observations indices; Sequence retains the one-based capture index. The initial invalid CLI key encoding run is retained in PriorRuns but excluded.",
    "This scenario uses real trusted TLS. Explicit SSECustomerKey and MD5 values are synthetic wire base64 fields, not real credentials.",
    "Buckets, role ARN, account, returned source versions and SSE-C ETags rebind to local outputs. Replica equality retains the native source version/ETag relationship, not a fixed opaque encryption ETag.",
    "At and Drain freeze local scheduling until each observed terminal state; one-second local advances are not AWS latency claims. Pending and committed data are reopened on both retained backends.",
    "Metadata mutation occurs after blocking destination writes. Only observed successful tag propagation is projected; payload remains the originally captured object.",
    "No additional SSE-C permissions or customer key are provided to the replication role. Native teardown and redundant polls remain evidence only."
  ],
  "Limitations": [
    "No CloudTrail, SQS or metrics resource was created. Failure-reason notification diagnostics are not measured; only returned source replication status and object API responses are measured.",
    "Polling windows are capture bounds, not AWS latency guarantees."
